# Sentinel file-role map for E156.   Format: <glob>  <role>
#
# Roles: shipped | record | scratch      (see F:/Sentinel/sentinel/io/roles.py)
#
#   shipped  code/docs a consumer receives, runs, or follows.  ALL rules apply.
#            This is the DEFAULT for anything not matched below -- a role map
#            that defaults to exempt is how a rule suite goes inert.
#   record   authored, kept for provenance, never executed: dated lane notes,
#            audit reports, session records.  An absolute path in one of these
#            is DATA ("the run happened at C:/Projects/x on pc2"), not a
#            portability break.
#   scratch  working files with no consumer: burn dirs, captured stderr.
#
# LAST MATCH WINS, so this file reads top-to-bottom as increasingly specific
# overrides.  Note that fnmatch's `*` crosses `/`, so `*.md` means EVERY
# markdown file; the shipped trees below are re-asserted after it on purpose.
#
# Adopting this moves no files.  A directory layout (notes/, _burn/) is the
# tidier long-term form but is not a precondition.
#
# Measured 2026-08-30 against the 155 BLOCK verdicts of P0-hardcoded-local-path:
#   record  127 (81.9%)   scratch 26 (16.8%)   shipped 2 (1.3%)

# ---- scratch -------------------------------------------------------------
_burn/**                                scratch
_tmp/**                                 scratch
_scratch/**                             scratch
.backups-2026-07-21/**                  scratch

# ---- record: authored notes and audit reports ----------------------------
# Every .md and .txt starts as a record; the shipped trees are restored below.
*.md                                    record
*.txt                                   record

# ---- shipped: restored after the broad record sweep ----------------------
README.md                               shipped
AGENTS.md                               shipped
CLAUDE.md                               shipped
CONTRIBUTING.md                         shipped
LICENSE                                 shipped
rewrite-workbook.txt                    shipped
requirements.lock                       shipped

docs/**                                 shipped
scripts/**                              shipped
paper/**                                shipped
outputs/**                              shipped
tests/**                                shipped
releases/**                             shipped
.github/**                              shipped

# Code is shipped wherever it lives (these come last so they win over *.md /
# *.txt for any note-shaped file that is actually executable).
**/*.py                                 shipped
**/*.js                                 shipped
**/*.ts                                 shipped
**/*.sh                                 shipped
**/*.ps1                                shipped
**/*.bat                                shipped
**/*.R                                  shipped
**/*.html                               shipped

# ...except inside a scratch tree, which stays scratch.
_burn/**                                scratch
_tmp/**                                 scratch
_scratch/**                             scratch
